    "officialListShortUrl": "https://www.irs.gov/tippedoccupations",
    "regulation": "Final regulations TD 10044, RIN 1545-BR63, 26 CFR 1.224-1(h) Table 1, scheduled for Federal Register publication 2026-04-13, effective 60 days after publication. Full text: https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-07104.pdf",
    "codeSystem": "Treasury Tipped Occupation Code (TTOC): a three-digit code. The leading digit is the category and the last two digits are the occupation within it. Eight categories: 101-110 Beverage and Food Service; 201-211 Entertainment and Events; 301-304 Hospitality and Guest Services; 401-409 Home Services; 501-510 Personal Services; 601-611 Personal Appearance and Wellness; 701-706 Recreation and Instruction; 801-810 Transportation and Delivery. Each row also carries a related BLS Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) code, illustrative examples, and a description. The illustrative examples are NOT exhaustive: an unlisted job that fits a TTOC's description qualifies.",
    "w2Linkage": "For tax year 2026 the employer reports the TTOC in new Form W-2 box 14b (up to two codes) alongside total cash tips in box 12 code TP. Source: 2026 General Instructions for Forms W-2 and W-3, https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/iw2w3.pdf",
    "howToRecheckAnnually": "The list is fixed by reference to occupations that received tips on or before 2024-12-31, so it is not an annually indexed figure, but Treasury may amend 26 CFR 1.224-1(h). Re-check the IRS list page above and search the Federal Register for amendments to 1.224-1 each filing season.",
    "fixedOn": "2026-08-15 — the 200-block was OFF BY ONE from code 205 onward because official TTOC 205 'Dancers' was absent, so a W-2 box 14b code of 205 was rendered as 'Musician or singer'. Realigned: 205 Dancers (new) and the six existing entries shifted up one to 206 Musicians and Singers, 207 Disc Jockeys Except Radio, 208 Entertainers and Performers, 209 Digital Content Creators, 210 Ushers Lobby Attendants and Ticket Takers, 211 Locker Room Coatroom and Dressing Room Attendants. Added the four other recorded missing rows: 509 Visual Artists, 510 Floral Designers, 611 Shoe and Leather Workers and Repairers, 810 Gas Pump Attendant. Count 66 -> 71, matching the official list. Codes and titles for the changed/added rows are taken verbatim from VERIFICATION-STATUS.md; keywords are search aids only and are not authoritative.",
    "titlesStillToAdopt": "Rows outside the 200-block and the four additions still carry the engine's shortened singular titles (e.g. 'Bartender' for official 'Bartenders'). VERIFICATION-STATUS.md confirms these are the SAME occupations — cosmetic only — but adopting the official strings verbatim remains advisable so a user can match what they see on IRS.gov. Two substantive wording gaps to close at the same time: official 506 is 'Pet and show animal caretakers' (this file: 'Pet caretaker') and official 103 is 'Food or beverage servers, non-restaurant' (this file: 'Food server, non-restaurant')."
  },
